title: MikroTik REST API: UPS
agents: mikrotik_rest_api
catalog: hw/network/mikrotik
license: GPL
distribution: check_mk
description:
 UPS connected to a MikroTik router via USB or serial ({/system/ups},
 needs the RouterOS package {ups.npk}). The agent reads the UPS list and
 runs {/system/ups/monitor once} for each UPS.

 Reported: power source (CRIT on battery by default), battery low (CRIT),
 battery needs replacement and output overloaded (WARN), battery charge
 (lower levels 50%/25%), remaining runtime (lower levels 10/5 min), output
 load (upper levels 80%/90%), temperature, input/output/battery voltage
 and frequency. All levels and states via the rule {MikroTik REST API: UPS}.

 Special agent {MikroTik RouterOS (mikrotik-rest-api)} in Setup >
 Agents > Other integrations, module "UPS".

 Added in mikrotik-rest-api 1.1.0 by Klaus Paulitsch.

item:
 The name of the UPS.

perfdata:
 Battery charge, runtime left, load, temperature, voltages, frequency.

inventory:
 One service per UPS that is not disabled.
